-- title:
--   Corollary 4.6 — every cluster point of the e-PSG iterates is a stationary point of (P)
-- statement:
--   Consider the fractional program
--   $$\min_{x\in S}\ \frac{f(x)}{g(x)},\qquad f=f^s+f^n,$$
--   on a finite-dimensional real Hilbert space $\mathcal H$, with $S$ nonempty, closed and convex, under Assumptions 1 and 2, and let $(x_n)$ be generated by Algorithm 1 (e-PSG) with parameters $\delta,\zeta>0$, $1-\sqrt\beta\,\zeta>0$, and $\bar\mu,\bar\kappa$ chosen as in Step 1 (under (BC) or, without it, $\bar\mu=\bar\kappa=0$), with the sublevel set $\{x\in S: f(x)/g(x)\le f(x_0)/g(x_0)\}$ bounded: these are the hypotheses of Theorem 4.5. Suppose further that
--
--   1. $\liminf_{n\to\infty}\tau_n=\bar\tau>0$;
--   2. Assumption 3 holds;
--   3. $g$ is strictly differentiable on an open set containing $S\cap\operatorname{dom} f$.
--
--   Then every cluster point $\bar x$ of $(x_n)$ is a stationary point of (P):
--   $$0\in\partial_L\Big(\frac fg+\iota_S\Big)(\bar x).$$
--
--   This upgrades Theorem 4.5(iii), which gives lifted stationarity of the cluster points, to stationarity in the sense of Definition 3.1(i); Theorem 5.5 uses it to identify the limit of the whole sequence.
--
--   **Formalization Note** The run of Algorithm 1, Assumptions 1 and 2, the Step 1 parameter ranges and the sublevel set are the published definitions of `FracPSG.Subseq.EPSG`, used exactly as in `FracPSG.Subseq.theorem_4_5_iii`, except that the corrective hypothesis `hgLip` of that theorem is not assumed. Strict differentiability of $g$ on $O$ is `HasStrictFDerivAt` at every point of $O$. Cluster points are `MapClusterPt`.
--
--   Differences from the source:
--   - encoding: lim inf τₙ = τ̄ > 0 → there is τ̄ > 0 with τₙ ≥ τ̄ for all large n; reason: equivalent: τₙ ≤ 1/δ is bounded, and a positive lim inf is exactly an eventual positive lower bound
--   - encoding: the hypotheses of Theorem 4.5 → the published chunk-01 hypotheses of FracPSG.Subseq.theorem_4_5_i–iii without its added hypothesis hgLip; reason: hgLip corrects Theorem 4.5(iii) for denominators with empty ∂_L g; here g is strictly differentiable on an open set containing S ∩ dom f, which contains every cluster point, so the printed corollary needs no correction
--   - generalization: g: H → (−∞, +∞] proper lower semicontinuous on H (problem (P), p. 1) → g : H → ℝ, positive on S and continuous on an open set containing S (published Assumption2), with no lower semicontinuity away from S; reason: only the values of g on a neighbourhood of S enter the algorithm and the conclusion; an extended-real g of the paper is finite and continuous near S, so it agrees there with a real-valued g of the Lean, and lower semicontinuity off S is never used (same convention as the published Theorem 4.5 items)
-- source:
--   Boţ, Dao, Li, Extrapolated Proximal Subgradient Algorithms for Nonconvex and Nonsmooth Fractional Programs, arXiv:2003.04124v2, p. 13, Corollary 4.6 (hypotheses of Theorem 4.5, p. 10; Assumption 3, p. 13)

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_NonconvexSplitting_Shared_LimitingSubdiff
import Definitions.Def_NonconvexSplitting_Shared_StandingAssumptions
import Definitions.Def_FracPSG_Subseq_Basic
import Definitions.Def_FracPSG_Subseq_EPSG
import Definitions.Def_FracPSG_Abstract_Supplement_Stationary
import Definitions.Def_FracPSG_Abstract_Supplement_Assumption3

open Filter Topology
open scoped InnerProductSpace

namespace FracPSG.Abstract.Supplement

open NonconvexSplitting.Shared FracPSG.Subseq

/-- Corollary 4.6 (Boţ–Dao–Li, arXiv:2003.04124v2, p. 13): under the hypotheses of Theorem 4.5
(problem (P) with `S` nonempty closed convex, Assumptions 1 and 2, a Step 1 parameter choice,
bounded `S₀`, a run of Algorithm 1), if moreover `liminf τₙ = τ̄ > 0` (here: `τₙ ≥ τ̄ > 0`
eventually), Assumption 3 holds and `g` is strictly differentiable at every point of an open set
containing `S ∩ dom f`, then every cluster point of the iterates is a stationary point of (P). -/
theorem corollary_4_6
    {N : ℕ} {S : Set (EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin N))}
    {fs : EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin N) → ℝ} {fn : EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin N) → EReal}
    {g : EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin N) → ℝ} {ℓ β δ ζ μbar κbar : ℝ}
    {x gs : ℕ → EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin N)} {τ κ μ : ℕ → ℝ}
    (hS : IsClosed S) (hSconv : Convex ℝ S)
    (hA1 : Assumption1 S fs fn ℓ) (hA2 : Assumption2 S g β)
    (hδ : 0 < δ) (hζ : 0 < ζ) (hβζ : 0 < 1 - Real.sqrt β * ζ) {m M : ℝ}
    (hpar : ParamsBC S (objF fs fn) g ℓ β δ ζ μbar κbar m M ∨ ParamsNoBC μbar κbar)
    (hrun : IsEPSGRun S fs fn g ℓ β δ ζ μbar κbar x gs τ κ μ)
    (hS0 : Bornology.IsBounded (S0 S (objF fs fn) g (x 0)))
    (hτ : ∃ τbar : ℝ, 0 < τbar ∧ ∀ᶠ n in atTop, τbar ≤ τ n)
    (hA3 : Assumption3 S fs fn g)
    (hgdiff : ∃ O : Set (EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin N)), IsOpen O ∧
      (∀ y ∈ S, objF fs fn y ≠ ⊤ → y ∈ O) ∧
      ∀ y ∈ O, ∃ L : EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin N) →L[ℝ] ℝ, HasStrictFDerivAt g L y) :
    ∀ xbar : EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin N), MapClusterPt xbar atTop x →
      IsStationary (objF fs fn) g S xbar := by sorry

end FracPSG.Abstract.Supplement
